# React Native Stack Conventions

## SDK + tooling

- **Expo SDK 52+** (managed workflow — escape to bare only if a native module forces it)
- **React Native 0.76+** with New Architecture enabled
- **TypeScript** strict mode: `strict: true`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes: true`
- **bun** package manager (not npm, not yarn, not pnpm)
- **Node** version pinned via `.nvmrc` (same as web's `frontend/.nvmrc`)

## Directory layout

```
src/
  app/                 (Expo Router screens — file-based routing)
  components/          (reusable UI components)
    ui/                (primitives: Button, Input, Card, Text, Heading, Badge)
    features/          (feature-specific composites)
  hooks/               (custom hooks; one per file)
    api/               (React Query hooks per backend resource)
    native/            (hooks wrapping Expo modules: biometric, push, camera)
  lib/                 (pure utility functions — synced from web)
    format.ts          (synced)
    fees.ts            (synced)
    state-machines/    (synced)
    storage/           (mobile-only: SecureStore + AsyncStorage wrappers)
    api-client.ts      (mobile-specific axios setup)
  schemas/             (zod validators — synced from web)
  constants/           (currency codes, networks, etc. — synced from web)
  types/               (API types — synced from web; mobile-specific in subfolders)
  services/            (HTTP service files per backend resource)
  store/               (Redux slices + Zustand stores)
  navigation/          (React Navigation config — types live here)
  native/              (low-level native module wrappers if needed)
  __tests__/           (top-level test helpers; per-file tests live next to source)
```

## Routing

- **Use Expo Router** (file-based) — same mental model as Next.js App Router; web developers transitioning to mobile will feel at home
- Layout files (`_layout.tsx`) for shared chrome
- Auth gate at root via `<AuthGuard />`
- Type-safe params via Expo Router's generated types

## State management

| Use case | Tool |
|---|---|
| Server state (anything from backend) | React Query (TanStack v5) |
| Global app state (auth, currency pref, theme) | Redux Toolkit (mirror web's pattern) |
| Ephemeral UI state (sheets, modals, toasts) | Zustand or `useState` |
| Form state | `react-hook-form` (same as web) |
| Validation | `zod` (same as web; schemas synced) |

## Styling

- **NativeWind v4** — Tailwind for RN. Use the same tokens as web.
- All colors via tokens (`bg-brand`, `text-foreground`, etc.) — no hardcoded hex
- Poppins font only (loaded via `expo-google-fonts/poppins`); splash holds until loaded
- Spacing scale matches web's `tailwind.config.ts` exactly
- Dark mode via `useColorScheme()` + Tailwind's `dark:` modifier — system + manual override

## Native modules

Prefer Expo SDK modules first (community-supported, managed builds work):

| Need | Module |
|---|---|
| Secure storage | `expo-secure-store` |
| Biometric | `expo-local-authentication` |
| Push notifications | `expo-notifications` (FCM + APNs) |
| Camera | `expo-camera` |
| Image picker | `expo-image-picker` |
| Image (caching) | `expo-image` (replaces RN `Image`) |
| QR scanning | `expo-barcode-scanner` |
| Linking | `expo-linking` |
| App state | `expo-application`, `expo-device` |
| Filesystem | `expo-file-system` |
| Sharing | `expo-sharing` |
| Splash | `expo-splash-screen` |
| Status bar | `expo-status-bar` |
| Crypto | `expo-crypto` |
| Haptics | `expo-haptics` |

Fall back to `react-native-*` community packages only when Expo doesn't cover the need (e.g. `@react-native-community/netinfo`, `@shopify/flash-list`, `@react-native-google-signin/google-signin`).

## API client pattern

```ts
// src/lib/api-client.ts
import axios from 'axios';
import { secureStorage } from './storage/secure';

const apiClient = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL,
  timeout: 30_000,
});

apiClient.interceptors.request.use(async (config) => {
  const token = await secureStorage.get('qic_access');
  if (token) {
    config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  }
  return config;
});

apiClient.interceptors.response.use(
  (r) => r,
  async (error) => {
    if (error.response?.status === 401) {
      // refresh logic mirrors web's frontend/src/lib/api-client.ts
      // ...
    }
    return Promise.reject(toApiError(error));
  },
);
```

Mirror the structure of `Qictrader/frontend/src/lib/api-client.ts` — same interceptor sequence, same retry semantics, same error mapping.

## Hooks pattern (one per file)

```ts
// src/hooks/api/use-wallet.ts
export function useWallet() {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['wallet'],
    queryFn: () => walletService.getAll(),
    staleTime: 30_000,
  });
}

export function useWithdraw() {
  const qc = useQueryClient();
  return useMutation({
    mutationFn: (input: WithdrawInput) => walletService.withdraw(input),
    onSuccess: () => { qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['wallet'] }); },
  });
}
```

## Forbidden patterns

- `View` with hardcoded color hex / pixel values — use NativeWind / tokens
- `console.log` left in committed code (Sentry breadcrumbs are fine; raw console isn't)
- `as any` to silence TypeScript
- `// @ts-ignore` ever
- `// @ts-expect-error` without a tracking ticket comment
- Empty `catch {}`
- `let _ = somePromise()`
- `AsyncStorage` for tokens (see `no-asyncstorage-for-secrets.mdc`)
- Direct `localStorage` references (web-only)
- Wagmi / Viem (web-only)

## Linting

ESLint config mirrors web's `eslint.config.mjs` with RN-specific rules added:
- `react-native/no-inline-styles`
- `react-native/no-color-literals`
- `react-native/no-unused-styles`
- `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`
- `@typescript-eslint/no-non-null-assertion`

## Build

- `bun run start` — dev server with Metro
- `bun run ios` — launch iOS simulator
- `bun run android` — launch Android emulator
- `bun run typecheck` — TS check
- `bun run lint` — ESLint
- `bun test` — Jest
- `bun run maestro` — E2E suite
- `eas build` — cloud builds (see `eas-deploy-only.mdc`)
